# Project Rules

## Project Shape
- This project is configured for SwarmForge with four Codex-backed agents: specifier, coder, refactorer, and architect.
- Project language: Lua 5.4, hosted by the Eggy editor (host runs on Windows; development on macOS / WSL Ubuntu).
- `EggyAPI.lua` / `EggyEditorAPI.lua` are third-party host-API boundaries; do not modify them.

## Command Mapping
- Upstream prompt text mentioning `bb test` / `bb coverage` / `bb acceptance` maps to `lua tools/cli.lua verify` / `lua tools/cli.lua verify --coverage` / `lua tools/cli.lua acceptance`. Never run bb/clj commands in this repo.
- The acceptance lane lives in tools/packages/acceptance with Gherkin specs under features/; extend it, do not rescaffold from upstream Clojure templates.
- Deployment uses tools/packages/ops/deploy.lua (Lua 5.4); there is no deploy.ps1.
- Hard floor: `lua tools/cli.lua verify` (slim) fully green before any push.

## Local Configuration
- Preserve project-local SwarmForge configuration under `swarmforge/`.
- Keep swarm state local under `.swarmforge/`, worktrees under `.worktrees/`, and shared scripts under `swarmforge/scripts/`.

## Handoffs
- Prefer terse, explicit handoffs that report state and request role-appropriate review. Do not include verifications or sender process narrative.

## Ownership
- Do not change another role's prompt or workflow ownership without explicit user direction.
